{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.IsolatedZeros","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge.q0_determined_of_analytic_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge.q0_determined_of_analytic_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge.lean#L125-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge.gate_does_not_determine_q0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge.gate_does_not_determine_q0","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge.lean#L92-L110","doc":"**The gate does not determine the substrate value.** For any gate set `S` with\n`q₀ ∉ S` and any two distinct values `v₁ ≠ v₂`, there exist two functions that\nagree with each other (and with the target `f`) at **every** point of `S` but\ndisagree at `q₀`.\n\nSo \"matches the Hecke row at all roots of unity\" is, by itself, consistent with\n*any* value at the substrate anchor. Determination requires an extra hypothesis\ntying `q₀` to `S` — rationality (the sibling's route, which then forces `f = 0`)\nor an analytic bridge. Absent that, the root-of-unity gate is silent at `q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge.q0_value_arbitrary_on_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge.q0_value_arbitrary_on_gate","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsToQ0Bridge.lean#L74-L90","doc":"**The gate value at `q₀` is arbitrary.** If the substrate point `q₀` is not\nitself in the gate set `S`, then for any target `f` and any prescribed value `v`\nthere is a function agreeing with `f` at every gate point yet taking the value `v`\nat `q₀`.\n\nThis is the formal price of leaving the analytic (rational) class: a candidate\nthat is merely *defined* at `q₀` — rather than analytically continued there —\ninherits **no** constraint from matching at roots of unity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}